This package installs LACT, a Linux GPU configuration and monitoring tool.

Enable the service:

  # ln -s /etc/sv/lactd /var/service/

Optional runtime dependencies:

  - clinfo:       Displays OpenCL-related GPU details.
  - Vulkan-Tools: Displays each GPU's Vulkan features and extensions.

Install them manually if you need them:

  # xbps-install -S clinfo Vulkan-Tools

Nvidia support:

GPU control on Nvidia hardware requires the proprietary Nvidia driver
with its CUDA libraries installed; the open-source nouveau driver is
not supported for this purpose.